WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.728 --> 00:00:18.418
The next evening Daisy and her dad went outside.

2
00:00:19.479 --> 00:00:21.280
Kaleem was waiting in their backyard.

3
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.862
"I brought a flashlight."

4
00:00:22.882 --> 00:00:24.803
"Thanks," Daisy said.

5
00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:27.506
"Dad's going to light the firepit for us."

6
00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:29.568
Beatrice buzzed over.

7
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.042
"Did you decide on an animal, Daisy?"

8
00:00:37.526 --> 00:00:39.187
yet," Daisy whispered back.

9
00:00:39.207 --> 00:00:41.990
"But I'll figure something out—I promise!"

10
00:00:45.353 --> 00:00:47.054
Daisy's dad lit the fire.

11
00:00:47.074 --> 00:00:49.436
"There you go, kids.

12
00:00:50.197 --> 00:00:51.538
It should help to keep the bugs away.

13
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.482
They're pretty bad this year."

14
00:00:55.502 --> 00:01:01.265
"Yeah." Kaleem waved away a few flying insects.

15
00:01:01.285 --> 00:01:04.187
"I have like ten mosquito bites already!"

16
00:01:05.248 --> 00:01:06.508
Daisy's dad chuckled.

17
00:01:06.528 --> 00:01:10.511
"I'll come back soon to check on you.

18
00:01:11.091 --> 00:01:12.372
Good luck with your bat watching."

19
00:01:12.392 --> 00:01:14.953
"Thanks," Daisy and Kaleem said.

20
00:01:20.817 --> 00:01:22.978
They sat down in lawn chairs by the fire.

21
00:01:23.818 --> 00:01:26.520
Beatrice settled onto the arm of Daisy's chair.

22
00:01:27.396 --> 00:01:31.117
Daisy told Kaleem what her parents had said about the disappearing bats.

23
00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:33.478
Kaleem's eyes went wide.

24
00:01:33.498 --> 00:01:35.778
"My parents said the same thing.

25
00:01:36.819 --> 00:01:38.459
What do you think happened to all the bats?"

26
00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:40.140
Daisy shrugged.

27
00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:41.700
"It's a mystery.

28
00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.921
But I think we can solve it.

29
00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:48.142
We just need to collect some clues."

30
00:01:49.022 --> 00:01:52.443
She spotted a mouse creeping past, heading for the woods.

31
00:01:53.103 --> 00:01:54.184
"Excuse me, mouse!"

32
00:01:54.804 --> 00:01:55.704
Daisy leaped up.

33
00:01:56.488 --> 00:01:57.789
"I have an important question.

34
00:01:58.309 --> 00:01:59.990
Have you seen any bats lately?"

35
00:02:01.692 --> 00:02:05.214
The mouse moved closer, keeping a wary eye on the fire.

36
00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:08.836
"No, but I mostly watch the sky for owls.

37
00:02:09.497 --> 00:02:10.598
They like to eat mice."

38
00:02:12.779 --> 00:02:15.581
The mouse scurried away as Daisy filled in Kaleem.

39
00:02:15.941 --> 00:02:18.643
A moment later an owl swooped low.

40
00:02:23.406 --> 00:02:26.028
Good thing that mouse got out of here," Kaleem said.

41
00:02:26.668 --> 00:02:27.529
Daisy nodded.

42
00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:32.051
Then she called to the owl and asked him about bats.

43
00:02:33.092 --> 00:02:34.352
The owl looked thoughtful.

44
00:02:34.833 --> 00:02:36.714
"I've seen a few recently."

45
00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:38.414
"You have?"

46
00:02:38.795 --> 00:02:39.495
Daisy said.

47
00:02:39.995 --> 00:02:41.876
She quickly told Kaleem the news.

48
00:02:41.896 --> 00:02:47.079
"Where?" "Deep in the forest," the owl said.

49
00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:50.361
"I don't think they come out this way much."

50
00:02:54.783 --> 00:02:58.290
interesting," Daisy said after the owl flew off.

51
00:02:59.071 --> 00:03:01.212
Kaleem nodded, looking thoughtful.

52
00:03:01.232 --> 00:03:05.756
"Yet our parents remember seeing bats flying around our yards before.

53
00:03:06.937 --> 00:03:07.838
So what changed?"

54
00:03:08.999 --> 00:03:13.182
Daisy jumped up, distracted by a few tiny flashes of light.

55
00:03:13.202 --> 00:03:15.744
"Look, Kaleem, fireflies!

56
00:03:19.047 --> 00:03:21.449
That's the first time I've seen any this spring."

57
00:03:22.469 --> 00:03:23.390
Kaleem smiled.

58
00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:25.512
"I love seeing them!

59
00:03:26.048 --> 00:03:28.249
Remember when I went to visit my cousins last summer?"

60
00:03:28.269 --> 00:03:30.509
"Yes," Daisy said.

61
00:03:30.529 --> 00:03:32.890
"They live on a big farm, right?"

62
00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:35.311
"Right," Kaleem said.

63
00:03:35.331 --> 00:03:37.931
"They have tons of fireflies there.

64
00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:39.652
We caught some in a jar."

65
00:03:40.932 --> 00:03:43.313
Beatrice buzzed loudly with alarm.

66
00:03:43.333 --> 00:03:46.454
"You did what?"

67
00:03:47.214 --> 00:03:50.335
Daisy laughed and told Kaleem what Beatrice had said.

68
00:03:50.355 --> 00:03:52.975
"Don't worry, Beatrice," Kaleem said.

69
00:03:52.995 --> 00:03:55.116
"We let them go after a few minutes.

70
00:03:55.736 --> 00:03:57.677
But it was cool to see them light up in the jar.

71
00:03:58.297 --> 00:04:00.238
It was like having a living flashlight!"

72
00:04:01.178 --> 00:04:04.880
Daisy watched the fireflies glowing dimly in her backyard.

73
00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.762
Then she glanced around at the houses surrounding hers.

74
00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:12.703
Light shone through the windows from interior rooms.

75
00:04:14.064 --> 00:04:17.765
It also shone from streetlamps and lights on porches and decks.

76
00:04:19.086 --> 00:04:22.087
Yet her backyard was a little darker than usual.

77
00:04:22.107 --> 00:04:24.662
"Kaleem, I've got it!"

78
00:04:24.943 --> 00:04:25.685
Daisy cried.

79
00:04:25.705 --> 00:04:28.291
"I just solved the missing bat mystery!"
